fix(writer): the printed commit step carries the uncommitted files a written feature manifest lists

Root cause of a Critic course that could never be read again (live Codex
greenfield, 2026-11-16): the commit step a sanctioned writer prints is built
from what changed during the writer run. The accepted-delivery receipt is
written by an earlier step and left uncommitted; materialize-architecture
only registers it in the feature manifest. The printed
git commit -F ... -- <list> therefore took the manifest alone, the commit
named a file it did not hold, and every later course read refused that
manifest revision (CCA-EVIDENCE-MODE).

Every file a manifest the writer wrote lists, that is still uncommitted in
the working tree, now joins the same step. A listed file that is committed
and clean, or absent, adds nothing. The commit-pipeline-owned route already
carried listed candidate evidence; this closes the other route, the one the
writer's own output tells the agent to run.

